{"attack": true, "case": "The mechanism's concluding assertion — 'It follows that the underlying structure was never relevant to the outcome at all' — is a non sequitur that contradicts the very evolutionary model it invokes. The described mechanism shifts rationality to population-level selection, but evolutionary selection requires a variation pool from which to select. That variation pool is generated by individual scientists' cognitive processes. If the 'underlying structure' of individual reasoning shapes which candidate theories enter the pool (the 'blind variation' input), then that structure is causally relevant to the outcome — it constrains the search space the selective filter operates on. An evolutionary-selection account therefore entails that the underlying structure of individual agency IS relevant to the outcome (it determines the variation distribution), not that it was 'never relevant.' The target's own mechanism thus undermines its own conclusion, making the dissolution internally incoherent.", "premise": "In an evolutionary selection model (blind variation + selective retention), the distribution of variations supplied to the selection filter is a causal determinant of the outcome, so the generative structure producing those variations is relevant to the outcome.", "premise_evidence": [{"block": "2e7ccfffa6de24", "quote": "Shifting the locus of rationality from the individual scientist's justification to the population-level dynamics of theory selection. The 'cost' is abandoning the idea that individual scientists must have a non-inductive *reason* for their choice; they merely participate in a blind variation and selective retention process. It follows that the underlying structure was never relevant to the outcome at all."}], "counterexample": ["An evolutionary search algorithm where the variation operator is a structured mutation kernel rather than uniform random noise: the structure of the variation operator determines which regions of the search space are explored, thereby affecting which solutions the selective filter can reach. Changing the variation structure changes the outcome distribution, so the underlying structure is relevant to the outcome even though selection happens at the population level."], "successor_question": "If the evolutionary analogy requires that individual cognitive structure shapes the variation pool from which selection operates, can the dissolution still avoid demanding some account of individual-level rationality in theory generation?"}